asr-000379
00:27:12.660 --> 00:27:15.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: that were released last January

asr-000380
00:27:15.660 --> 00:27:19.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: by the PQF National Coordinating Council.

asr-000381
00:27:19.660 --> 00:27:20.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Next slide.

asr-000382
00:27:20.660 --> 00:27:22.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: TESDA is scaling AI,

asr-000383
00:27:22.660 --> 00:27:26.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: upscaling for BPO and digital jobs

asr-000384
00:27:26.660 --> 00:27:31.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: as a fear that the country has

asr-000385
00:27:31.660 --> 00:27:35.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: about AI disruption for jobs.

asr-000386
00:27:35.660 --> 00:27:37.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: We're trying to make sure

asr-000387
00:27:37.660 --> 00:27:41.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: that as many of our BPO's employees,

asr-000388
00:27:41.660 --> 00:27:42.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: for example,

asr-000389
00:27:42.660 --> 00:27:43.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: are AI-enabled

asr-000390
00:27:43.660 --> 00:27:45.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: so that they can go with the times.

asr-000391
00:27:45.660 --> 00:27:46.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: At the moment,

asr-000392
00:27:46.660 --> 00:27:49.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: 34,766 beneficiaries

asr-000393
00:27:49.660 --> 00:27:52.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: and institution-based AI and data courses

asr-000394
00:27:52.660 --> 00:27:54.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: have been identified.

asr-000395
00:27:54.660 --> 00:27:56.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: And we have been involved

asr-000396
00:27:56.660 --> 00:27:59.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: in crafting the AI upscaling roadmap,

asr-000397
00:27:59.660 --> 00:28:01.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: which aims to achieve widespread,

asr-000398
00:28:01.660 --> 00:28:03.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: or as widespread as possible,

asr-000399
00:28:03.660 --> 00:28:05.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: AI literacy

asr-000400
00:28:05.660 --> 00:28:07.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: to ensure that the country shifts

asr-000401
00:28:07.660 --> 00:28:09.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: from being an AI consumer

asr-000402
00:28:09.660 --> 00:28:12.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: to in fact being an AI builder.

asr-000403
00:28:12.660 --> 00:28:15.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: 10,000 BPO workers are being upscaled in AI

asr-000404
00:28:15.660 --> 00:28:18.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: through enterprise-based training.

asr-000405
00:28:18.660 --> 00:28:22.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So that's 34,766 for institution-based,

asr-000406
00:28:22.660 --> 00:28:25.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: an additional 10,000 for BPO workers

asr-000407
00:28:25.660 --> 00:28:27.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: for enterprise-based training

asr-000408
00:28:27.660 --> 00:28:29.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: for around 44,000.

asr-000409
00:28:29.660 --> 00:28:32.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: This is in addition to any other

asr-000410
00:28:32.660 --> 00:28:36.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: institution-based trainings

asr-000411
00:28:36.660 --> 00:28:37.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: and micro-credentials

asr-000412
00:28:37.660 --> 00:28:39.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: that we are rolling out.

asr-000413
00:28:39.660 --> 00:28:42.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: TESDA has also been very much a part

asr-000414
00:28:42.660 --> 00:28:44.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: of building the talent pipeline

asr-000415
00:28:44.660 --> 00:28:46.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: for semiconductors and electronics industry,

asr-000416
00:28:46.660 --> 00:28:47.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: which after all,

asr-000417
00:28:47.660 --> 00:28:49.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: is one of the largest,

asr-000418
00:28:49.660 --> 00:28:51.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: if not the largest,

asr-000419
00:28:51.660 --> 00:28:54.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: manufactured goods exports of the country.

asr-000420
00:28:54.660 --> 00:28:58.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: The Philippines Semiconductor Electronics Industry Roadmap

asr-000421
00:28:58.660 --> 00:29:00.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: has just recently been launched.

asr-000422
00:29:00.660 --> 00:29:02.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: And the roadmap targets

asr-000423
00:29:02.660 --> 00:29:06.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: $70 billion in semiconductor revenues

asr-000424
00:29:06.660 --> 00:29:10.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: and $40 billion in electronics revenues by 2030.

asr-000425
00:29:10.660 --> 00:29:15.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: And that growth that's been dictated by government

asr-000426
00:29:15.660 --> 00:29:16.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: will require skills

asr-000427
00:29:16.660 --> 00:29:20.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: will require skilled workforce.

asr-000428
00:29:20.660 --> 00:29:23.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: 140,000 have already been assessed

asr-000429
00:29:23.660 --> 00:29:25.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: on electronics assembly skills

asr-000430
00:29:25.660 --> 00:29:27.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: since January 2025.

asr-000431
00:29:27.660 --> 00:29:31.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: This is in compliance

asr-000432
00:29:31.660 --> 00:29:33.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: with the advisory council

asr-000433
00:29:33.660 --> 00:29:35.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: created under AO39,

asr-000434
00:29:35.660 --> 00:29:38.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: which has requested that TESDA

asr-000435
00:29:38.660 --> 00:29:42.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: provide skills training for 128,000 workers

asr-000436
00:29:42.660 --> 00:29:45.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: for the sector actually by 2028,

asr-000437
00:29:45.660 --> 00:29:46.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: I believe.

asr-000438
00:29:46.660 --> 00:29:48.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So we're slightly above schedule

asr-000439
00:29:48.660 --> 00:29:49.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: or ahead of schedule

asr-000440
00:29:49.660 --> 00:29:51.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: in terms of number of beneficiaries.

asr-000441
00:29:51.660 --> 00:29:53.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Our next piece is trying to make sure,

asr-000442
00:29:53.660 --> 00:29:54.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: in fact,

asr-000443
00:29:54.660 --> 00:29:56.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: that they are appropriately linked

asr-000444
00:29:56.660 --> 00:29:59.660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: to the right qualifications requested.

asr-000445
00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:21.220
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: By industry and at the right levels. So along that line, we have also piloted a level 5 diploma program skills ladder with engineering degrees in semiconductors and electronics with CHED piloted in Cebu with, I believe, 18 higher education institutions in Region 7.

asr-000446
00:30:22.640 --> 00:30:23.860
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Next slide.

asr-000447
00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:43.200
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: For the next slide, in conjunction with our special provisions in the 2026 GAHA, TESDA is upskilling daycare workers and partnering with LGUs for local skills needs.

asr-000448
00:30:43.640 --> 00:30:54.260
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So far, 9,989 CDWs were served under the ECCD program with ongoing training for at least 1,000 to 2,000 more.

asr-000449
00:30:55.180 --> 00:30:59.200
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: And we aim to train an additional 9,231.

asr-000450
00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:05.300
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: CDWs in 2027 in accordance, in fact, with the new ECCD law.

asr-000451
00:31:06.600 --> 00:31:11.800
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: We have also piloted waste management training, for example, with LGUs.

asr-000452
00:31:12.300 --> 00:31:17.340
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: And here's an example with Coca-Cola Foundation and the city of Naga.

asr-000453
00:31:20.020 --> 00:31:21.620
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Next slide.

asr-000454
00:31:22.620 --> 00:31:27.820
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So ito po yung isang tinanong ni Senator Joel kanina.

asr-000455
00:31:28.000 --> 00:31:29.900
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: The employment rate of TVET graduates.

asr-000456
00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:37.060
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: In 2025, was at 81.64% based on our survey methods.

asr-000457
00:31:38.000 --> 00:31:48.600
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: We are trying to scale up E-BET because E-BET graduates have a employment rate of almost 90% based on our data.

asr-000458
00:31:49.740 --> 00:31:59.060
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: And as of August 2026, 1,299 E-BET programs have been registered as part of our implementation.

asr-000459
00:31:59.100 --> 00:31:59.940
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: It's also part of our implementation.

asr-000460
00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:20.640
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So we have the World Bank project, Senator Villanueva, to make sure that we can further granularize and expand and strengthen our surveying methods as well as use the skills passport to track and encode data sets of training completely, totally to trabaho as much as possible.

asr-000461
00:32:22.000 --> 00:32:23.220
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Next slide.

asr-000462
00:32:23.220 --> 00:32:29.420
Senator Joel Villanueva: The entrance of E-BET, I mean E-BET clients.

asr-000463
00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:33.000
Senator Joel Villanueva: They are, when they came in, hindi pa sila employed.

asr-000464
00:32:33.840 --> 00:32:34.620
Senator Joel Villanueva: Or they are...

asr-000465
00:32:34.620 --> 00:32:35.080
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Iba po.

asr-000466
00:32:35.600 --> 00:32:46.320
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So the training modalities of, pwede pong upskilling sila, pwede pong silang apprenticeship, pwede pong silang general E-BET.

asr-000467
00:32:46.620 --> 00:32:50.740
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So some of them are already employed, but some of them are not.

asr-000468
00:32:51.380 --> 00:32:53.600
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: We can give you, sir, the breakdown if you wish.

asr-000469
00:32:54.460 --> 00:32:55.140
Senator Joel Villanueva: Sige, thank you.

asr-000470
00:32:55.160 --> 00:32:55.480
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Sige po.

asr-000471
00:32:55.520 --> 00:32:56.040
Senator Joel Villanueva: Please proceed, thank you.

asr-000472
00:32:57.260 --> 00:32:59.260
Senator Joel Villanueva: Baby ho ninyo ang E-BET lo eh, so.

asr-000473
00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:05.500
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So next slide, please.

asr-000474
00:33:05.500 --> 00:33:09.500
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: This one naman po is our flexible delivery modalities.

asr-000475
00:33:10.680 --> 00:33:14.920
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Favorite program din po ni Senator Villanueva, ang TESDA online program.

asr-000476
00:33:16.200 --> 00:33:23.500
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: We would like to point out that 1.6 million learners have enrolled in 225 courses.

asr-000477
00:33:24.720 --> 00:33:29.500
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Courses on AI fundamentals and environmental literacy are now actually available.

asr-000478
00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:36.100
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Available on TUP as well as financial literacy, entrepreneurship, among others.

asr-000479
00:33:36.920 --> 00:33:53.140
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: And in fact, TESDA recorded 91,905 enrollments in AI-related courses alone, including industry co-developed courses with Microsoft, IBM, and we have two or three other partners, in fact.

asr-000480
00:33:55.380 --> 00:33:59.980
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: There's a sample of potential courses available in TUP.

asr-000481
00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:12.020
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: We have complete full NC qualifications online, as well as short-term courses that might be more life-skills oriented and not necessarily job or employment specific.

asr-000482
00:34:13.880 --> 00:34:15.540
Senator Joel Villanueva: Assessments being done online?

asr-000483
00:34:15.960 --> 00:34:16.500
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: No, sir.

asr-000484
00:34:16.600 --> 00:34:19.860
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So the assessment is still, they still have to go walk-in.

asr-000485
00:34:20.280 --> 00:34:20.700
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Yes, sir.

asr-000486
00:34:24.240 --> 00:34:29.220
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: The next slide is our ongoing SIPTIVETS project.

asr-000499
00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:42.820
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: With ADB, in order to expand our TIVET capacity nationwide through regional innovation centers and potentially developing them into full-fledged polytechnics.

asr-000500
00:34:44.500 --> 00:34:47.160
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: There are meant to be three batches.

asr-000501
00:34:47.800 --> 00:34:53.060
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Two batches are actually ongoing, covering eight Arctic projects now under construction.

asr-000502
00:34:53.580 --> 00:34:58.220
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Batch one is targeted to be completed by the fourth quarter of this year.

asr-000503
00:34:58.380 --> 00:34:59.560
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: And batch two

asr-000504
00:34:59.560 --> 00:35:00.720
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: In 2027.

asr-000505
00:35:01.260 --> 00:35:07.320
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Batch three is ongoing with a new site in Negros Island region.

asr-000506
00:35:07.320 --> 00:35:15.680
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: They're all designed to be finished by the end of 2027 or the first quarter of 2028 at the latest.

asr-000507
00:35:19.240 --> 00:35:20.560
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Next slide.

asr-000508
00:35:21.320 --> 00:35:29.320
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: With our convergence, Mr. Chair, with OWWA and DMW, TESDA has been bringing free assessments

asr-000509
00:35:29.560 --> 00:35:37.040
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: to our OFWs as well as boosting skills of repatriated OFWs that come back.

asr-000510
00:35:37.040 --> 00:35:44.480
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: The TESDA overseas assessment program brings skills assessment and national certification directly to Filipino workers abroad.

asr-000511
00:35:45.200 --> 00:35:53.060
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: And we have current partners in Saudi Arabia, UAE, Singapore, Hong Kong, Malaysia, Qatar, Kuwait, and South Korea.

asr-000512
00:35:53.300 --> 00:35:59.000
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: With more countries being developed upon the request, in fact, of OWWA and DMW themselves.

asr-000515
00:35:59.560 --> 00:36:13.940
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Italy is already tentatively scheduled. New Zealand and London are under exploration as the demand for overseas assessment for OFWs increase.

asr-000516
00:36:13.940 --> 00:36:33.600
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: As part of our harmonization and again as part of the EDCOM recommendations, Mr. Chair, we have assessed 427,000 senior high school learners to boost job readiness of K-12 graduates.

asr-000517
00:36:33.600 --> 00:36:43.920
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: We have 6,143 teachers trained to become assessors since 2024 with more intended.

asr-000518
00:36:43.940 --> 00:37:07.400
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: For 2027, TESDA is proposing to train 4,888 teachers in their NC courses and in fact 23,845 teachers in training methodology to deliver in the TechPro programs in the strengthened senior high school, which will be rolled out for grade 12 this school year.

asr-000519
00:37:11.840 --> 00:37:13.520
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: We are also

asr-000520
00:37:13.520 --> 00:37:21.940
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: opening ladders as part of the seamless pathways recommended by One Education with CHED, on the other hand.

asr-000521
00:37:22.220 --> 00:37:43.500
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: We have Philippine credit transfer systems, which are ladderized for dental hygiene, agriculture and biosystems engineering, midwifery, pharmacy, and ongoing for approval are hospitality and tourism management, radiologic technologies, nutrition and dietetics.

asr-000522
00:37:43.520 --> 00:37:44.940
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Among others.

asr-000523
00:37:45.100 --> 00:37:53.820
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So this is an ongoing program that we are rolling out in accordance with the ladderization law.

asr-000524
00:37:54.620 --> 00:38:02.140
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: PCTS guidelines are under development for ECCD, medical technology, occupational therapy, and physical therapy programs.

asr-000525
00:38:02.260 --> 00:38:08.100
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Again, in compliance, Mr. Chair, with the recommendations of EDCOM as well.

asr-000526
00:38:09.440 --> 00:38:13.500
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: We are trying to increase the number of HEIs

asr-000527
00:38:13.540 --> 00:38:21.400
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: that will also roll out both TVI programs and/or recognize Philippine credit transfer systems.

asr-000528
00:38:22.840 --> 00:38:25.720
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So our 2027 proposed budget.

asr-000529
00:38:25.860 --> 00:38:35.560
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: All that, Mr. Chair, is to point out how little funding we have in order to address the needs and the demands that we are held accountable for.

asr-000530
00:38:35.560 --> 00:38:35.640
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Okay.

asr-000531
00:38:41.420 --> 00:38:42.100
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So,

asr-000532
00:38:42.500 --> 00:38:43.500
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: as I said,

asr-000533
00:38:43.520 --> 00:38:45.540
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Highlight of the history of our budget.

asr-000534
00:38:48.100 --> 00:38:51.940
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: TESDA received its largest budget on record in 2026,

asr-000535
00:38:52.560 --> 00:38:59.180
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: the same year that the Philippines devoted the highest share or percentage of its GDP to education in its history,

asr-000536
00:38:59.340 --> 00:39:05.720
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: where 2.2% of the total education budget in 2026 was allocated to TESDA.

asr-000537
00:39:06.320 --> 00:39:10.800
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: For NEP in 2027, Mr. Chair, bumaba po kami to 1.8.

asr-000538
00:39:10.800 --> 00:39:16.200
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: 1.88% na lang ng full education budget.

asr-000539
00:39:16.660 --> 00:39:21.600
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: And as you pointed out, yes po, yung 2.2 naging 1.88.

asr-000540
00:39:22.180 --> 00:39:30.980
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: At gaya po ng sinabi ninyo, almost 20% po ang binaba ng NEP 2027 sa GAA 2026.

asr-000541
00:39:31.680 --> 00:39:34.900
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Higher budget is key to sustaining TESDA's momentum,

asr-000542
00:39:34.900 --> 00:39:39.440
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: as well as our ability to address the Lifelong Learning Framework Act, Mr. Chair,

asr-000543
00:39:39.440 --> 00:39:46.880
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: for that entire, your entire workforce age population.

asr-000544
00:39:47.640 --> 00:39:56.100
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: The 2027 NEP, in fact, is 46.8% lower than the proposed TESDA budget,

asr-000545
00:39:57.420 --> 00:40:02.140
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: and 20% lower than GAA 2026.

asr-000546
00:40:04.620 --> 00:40:09.140
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Our TESDA utilization by September 2026 is actually,

asr-000547
00:40:09.440 --> 00:40:12.600
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: higher compared to the same period last year.

asr-000548
00:40:12.780 --> 00:40:16.620
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: We have recurring problems, Mr. Chair.

asr-000549
00:40:17.720 --> 00:40:24.840
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Our capital outlay from the SIPTIVET projects and the,

asr-000550
00:40:25.420 --> 00:40:28.280
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: for late release, for example, of funds,

asr-000551
