TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Mr. Chair,

asr-002706
02:29:27.480 --> 02:29:28.520
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: if your permission,

asr-002707
02:29:28.700 --> 02:29:30.040
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: I would like another voice.

asr-002708
02:29:30.160 --> 02:29:31.880
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Kanina pa kasi ako sumasagot.

asr-002709
02:29:32.260 --> 02:29:34.420
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Si DDG Galo will respond.

asr-002710
02:29:34.540 --> 02:29:35.440
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Si Galo, okay yan.

asr-002711
02:29:35.500 --> 02:29:36.480
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Malakas kumain yan.

asr-002712
02:29:38.160 --> 02:29:39.280
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: Thank you, Mr. President.

asr-002713
02:29:39.620 --> 02:29:41.400
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: With the permission of our good secretary,

asr-002714
02:29:42.120 --> 02:29:44.000
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: I will respond, Mr. President.

asr-002715
02:29:44.540 --> 02:29:45.940
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: Mr. President, you are right.

asr-002716
02:29:46.640 --> 02:29:47.940
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: We recognize po

asr-002717
02:29:47.940 --> 02:29:49.100
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: the risk

asr-002718
02:29:49.100 --> 02:29:49.640
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: risk

asr-002719
02:29:49.640 --> 02:29:53.140
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: that is brought by AI

asr-002720
02:29:53.140 --> 02:29:55.880
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: to our labor force.

asr-002721
02:29:56.280 --> 02:29:58.580
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: Depending on who you ask,

asr-002722
02:29:59.180 --> 02:30:02.360
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: the numbers vary,

asr-002731
02:30:02.360 --> 02:30:15.200
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: But more or less around 30 percent, Mr. Chair, of our labor force and jobs are at risk, will be transformed or exposed to AI.

asr-002732
02:30:15.200 --> 02:30:30.180
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: And we are very thankful, Mr. President, for the support of you and the Senate for the inclusion of a budget in the 2026 GAAA to support upskilling on AI.

asr-002733
02:30:30.180 --> 02:30:44.180
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: Mr. President, we are happy to report that for 2026, for data and AI skills,

asr-002734
02:30:44.580 --> 02:30:51.740
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: we have already allocated around 30,000 slots.

asr-002735
02:30:55.380 --> 02:31:09.200
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: And for semiconductors, Mr. Chair, we have here already allocations for around 6,000 slots, Mr. President.

asr-002736
02:31:10.820 --> 02:31:14.200
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: Ongoing pa po, Mr. President, ang pag-implementation.

asr-002737
02:31:14.580 --> 02:31:21.700
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: At natin ang mga programa na ito, we are scaling up our AI upskilling through partners like STI,

asr-002738
02:31:23.660 --> 02:31:32.840
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: nationwide networks of institutions that will deliver the courses, but also through Test the Online program, our e-learning platform,

asr-002739
02:31:33.540 --> 02:31:39.820
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: where already we have around 90,000 enrollments in AI courses, Mr. President.

asr-002740
02:31:41.340 --> 02:31:43.420
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: Tuloy-tuloy po ito, Mr. President.

asr-002741
02:31:43.420 --> 02:31:43.520
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: Thank you, Mr. President.

asr-002742
02:31:44.580 --> 02:31:51.300
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: And we hope to continue to be able to do this in 2027 with support of the Senate.

asr-002743
02:31:51.640 --> 02:31:52.080
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: Thank you, po.

asr-002744
02:31:52.460 --> 02:31:57.380
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: DDG, itong you mentioned 30% of jobs at risk.

asr-002745
02:31:58.120 --> 02:32:06.540
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, based on statistics, mayroon tayong 49 million workforce.

asr-002746
02:32:07.100 --> 02:32:10.740
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, 30% is about 10 million, more or less.

asr-002747
02:32:10.740 --> 02:32:13.740
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, in other words, 10 million of our...

asr-002748
02:32:14.580 --> 02:32:20.280
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: 10 million of the workforce is at risk of being affected by artificial intelligence.

asr-002749
02:32:20.420 --> 02:32:20.900
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yes, Mr. President.

asr-002750
02:32:20.900 --> 02:32:26.100
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But, obviously, maliit pa lang yung ating na-upskill, no?

asr-002751
02:32:26.580 --> 02:32:28.420
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Only 30,000 lang.

asr-002752
02:32:29.120 --> 02:32:35.920
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, in your analysis, of course, we need more funds to upgrade.

asr-002753
02:32:36.360 --> 02:32:43.800
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But in your analysis, what should be the priority in terms of protecting jobs from AI?

asr-002754
02:32:44.580 --> 02:32:46.700
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: For example, BPO.

asr-002755
02:32:47.360 --> 02:32:53.620
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kasi BPO, mayroon tayong about 1.5, 1.6 million employees.

asr-002756
02:32:54.280 --> 02:32:57.700
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And marami sa kanila mga entry-level jobs, no?

asr-002757
02:32:57.740 --> 02:32:59.440
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kasi puro voice calls.

asr-002758
02:33:00.100 --> 02:33:06.920
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And I am predicting that AI will have a massive effect on them.

asr-002759
02:33:07.060 --> 02:33:10.380
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Dahil next time, kausap na ng tao, artificial intelligence.

asr-002760
02:33:10.380 --> 02:33:13.320
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, for example, BPO, particular, no?

asr-002761
02:33:13.620 --> 02:33:14.380
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: How do we...

asr-002762
02:33:14.580 --> 02:33:20.240
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: How do we help the BPO industry survive the AI revolution

asr-002763
02:33:20.240 --> 02:33:27.980
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: so that AI will be part of the BPO industry and still grow our BPO industry?

asr-002764
02:33:29.940 --> 02:33:33.400
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: Mr. President, we are following the AI upskilling roadmap

asr-002765
02:33:33.400 --> 02:33:40.480
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: that we crafted together with the Commission on Higher Education

asr-002766
02:33:40.480 --> 02:33:43.920
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: and the Analytics and AI Association of the Philippines.

asr-002767
02:33:44.580 --> 02:33:51.140
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: So, kasama po sa roadmap na ito, ang efforts at plano natin to...

asr-002768
02:33:51.140 --> 02:33:52.000
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: So, mayroon tayong roadmap?

asr-002769
02:33:52.160 --> 02:33:52.460
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: Yes, sir.

asr-002770
02:33:52.460 --> 02:33:52.860
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: In other words?

asr-002771
02:33:52.900 --> 02:33:53.180
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: Yes, sir.

asr-002772
02:33:53.180 --> 02:33:53.280
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: Okay.

asr-002773
02:33:53.940 --> 02:34:02.300
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Can you describe to us ano ba yung mga skills, upskilling, or even reskilling ng AI skills?

asr-002774
02:34:02.580 --> 02:34:03.540
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Can you...

asr-002775
02:34:03.540 --> 02:34:08.440
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kasi, to be honest about it, like kami dito, we just use it for research.

asr-002776
02:34:08.480 --> 02:34:08.780
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yes, sir.

asr-002777
02:34:08.780 --> 02:34:14.420
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But what type of upskilling or even reskilling is TESTA doing to...

asr-002778
02:34:14.420 --> 02:34:16.900
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Let's say, the BPO industry or the other industries?

asr-002779
02:34:17.680 --> 02:34:23.700
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: Sir, the roadmap segmentizes our population and our labor market and labor force

asr-002780
02:34:23.700 --> 02:34:30.880
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: into basically three segments that need, first, literacy,

asr-002781
02:34:30.880 --> 02:34:37.640
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: which is foundational AI skills and awareness.

asr-002782
02:34:38.100 --> 02:34:44.120
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: Next will be a segment for more specialized jobs,

asr-002783
02:34:44.420 --> 02:34:50.940
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: and then, lastly, Mr. Chair, is really advanced courses

asr-002784
02:34:50.940 --> 02:35:00.840
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: to equip a segment of our labor force to become builders of AI platforms and AI systems.

asr-002785
02:35:01.620 --> 02:35:05.900
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: Not just consumers of AI, but as builders of AI.

asr-002786
02:35:06.440 --> 02:35:10.840
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: At yan din po ang isinusulong natin sa TESTA, Mr. Chair.

asr-002787
02:35:11.260 --> 02:35:13.540
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: While we started this year with...

asr-002788
02:35:13.540 --> 02:35:13.880
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: Yes.

asr-002789
02:35:13.880 --> 02:35:19.040
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: Around 30,000 slots for AI literacy and for foundational skills,

asr-002790
02:35:19.640 --> 02:35:24.320
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: next year, we are hoping to move towards more specialized and advanced courses

asr-002791
02:35:24.320 --> 02:35:31.340
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: to equip segments of our labor force to build AI systems.

asr-002792
02:35:32.240 --> 02:35:39.940
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: Sa BPO sector po, this means that they will also be able to provide higher value services,

asr-002793
02:35:39.940 --> 02:35:42.180
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: not just customer service,

asr-002794
02:35:42.720 --> 02:35:42.940
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: but also to create...

asr-002795
02:35:43.880 --> 02:35:46.680
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: to create products for clients abroad.

asr-002796
02:35:47.400 --> 02:35:50.880
TESDA Deputy Director General Galo B. Glino III: Ayan po ang kasama sa roadmap natin, Mr. Chair.

asr-002797
02:35:51.960 --> 02:36:01.100
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: For 2027, is this roadmap funded, adequately funded?

asr-002798
02:36:01.740 --> 02:36:09.580
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kasi nakita ko dito yung TWSP bumaba by 45%.

asr-002799
02:36:09.580 --> 02:36:12.580
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: From 3.6 billion, naging...

asr-002800
02:36:13.880 --> 02:36:27.980
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I think it's 3.6 billion next year, no?

asr-002801
02:36:28.020 --> 02:36:28.720
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: In budget.

asr-002802
02:36:29.140 --> 02:36:31.440
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, bumaba siya by 45%.

asr-002803
02:36:31.440 --> 02:36:34.680
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, it was mas malaki siya last year.

asr-002804
02:36:34.680 --> 02:36:41.400
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, in other words, with that roadmap, maganda meron tayong roadmap,

asr-002805
02:36:42.000 --> 02:36:43.680
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: pero bumaba naman yung ating...

asr-002806
02:36:43.880 --> 02:36:45.520
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: scholarship for AI,

asr-002807
02:36:46.220 --> 02:36:54.400
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: how will this affect the upskilling and reskilling program of our workforce?

asr-002808
02:36:55.260 --> 02:36:58.340
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Malit na nga dati, lumit pa ngayon,

asr-002809
02:36:59.080 --> 02:37:01.880
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: and there's a big chance na maapektuhan itong...

asr-002810
02:37:02.880 --> 02:37:04.880
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I just want to make it...

asr-002811
02:37:04.880 --> 02:37:09.860
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I just want to make the BPO industry as an example

asr-002812
02:37:09.860 --> 02:37:13.860
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: kasi siya yung ating saving grace for our economy.

asr-002813
02:37:13.880 --> 02:37:18.880
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, baka magkaroon tayo ng malaking problema

asr-002814
02:37:18.880 --> 02:37:23.300
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: kung hindi natin pupondohan itong AI upskilling and reskilling natin.

asr-002815
02:37:24.420 --> 02:37:28.500
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: We're looking for TESDA to really bridge that gap.

asr-002816
02:37:28.780 --> 02:37:29.260
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Yes, sir.

asr-002817
02:37:29.300 --> 02:37:35.940
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: The gap meaning from our present low-value BPO industry

asr-002818
02:37:35.940 --> 02:37:39.540
